        "subject": "LU-15444 osp: take destroy RPC version at llog write",
        "message": "LU-15444 osp: take destroy RPC version at llog write\n\nA remote MDT applies OUT requests in RPC version order.  A sub\ntransaction used to get its version at its first update llog write\nin llog_osd_write_rec(), under the llog lock, so the version order\nmatched the llog index order.  Since LU-16159 osp_md_destroy() takes\nthe version during execution, before llog_add(), so a concurrent\ntransaction can add a lower llog index with a higher version.  The\nremote MDT then applies the header, bitmap and tail writes of the\ntwo appends in reverse order.  After a remote error,\nllog_cat_refresh() reads back a tail that is behind a set bitmap\nbit, and the next append hits the LBUG in llog_osd_write_rec():\n\"index N already set in llog bitmap\".  The paused destroy also holds\nback every later update to that MDT until it reaches trans stop.\n\nOnly mark the request in osp_md_destroy().  osp_trans_stop() takes\nthe version if no write took it, so a destroy without llog write is\nstill sent after earlier writes.\n\nAdd recovery-small/169.  It pauses a striped directory rmdir before\nits update llog write (new OBD_FAIL_UPDATE_LOG_DELAY) while a striped\nmkdir adds a record, then checks the llog index and RPC version order\nin the MDT0000 debug log.\n\nFixes: 5a5bd5b4dafa (\"LU-16159 osp: destroy should not overtake writes\")\nHPE-bug-id: LUS-12774\nSigned-off-by: Alexander Boyko <alexander.boyko@hpe.com>\nAssisted-by: DSH:claude-opus-5.5\nChange-Id: I2762dcd1eefc81be9eadfd7a426cbce9c5e6de59\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
